course: dictionary
lesson: 15139
title: Scarcity: when there is not enough
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Scarcity means there is not enough of something that people need or want. Look for clues in the words around it. «During the drought, there was a scarcity of water in the village.» The drought is the clue: when rain stops, there is less water, so scarcity means a shortage.
explain: Scarcity often appears in phrases like «water scarcity» or «scarcity of food». Ask yourself: is there enough? If the answer is no, you have found scarcity. Try your meaning in the sentence: «There was not enough water in the village» still makes sense.
explain: In economics, scarcity is a bigger idea. Resources are limited, so people have to choose what to do with them. «With food in scarcity, the shop raised its prices» shows what can happen when there is little of something people want.
fact: Scarcity means there is not enough of something that people need or want.
fact: «Water scarcity» means there is not enough water for people, animals and crops.
fact: «Scarcity of food» means there is too little food for everyone.
fact: In economics, scarcity means resources are limited, so people must choose.
fact: When something is scarce, its price can go up, because many people want it and there is not much to buy.
exercise: «During the drought, there was a scarcity of water in the village.» What does scarcity mean here? | A river that runs very fast | A new well full of clean water | Too much rain falling at once | *Not enough water
exercise: Why might prices go up when there is food scarcity? | Shops close because it is raining | *Many people want the food, but there is not much of it | Nobody in the town likes to eat | Food is always given away for free
exercise: Which phrase means there is too little food for everyone? | Food fight | Food festival | *Food scarcity | Food court
test: In economics, what does scarcity show about resources? | Resources are only for rich people | Resources are endless and free for everyone | Resources are only found in shops | *Resources are limited, so people must choose
test: Which sentence uses scarcity correctly? | *Water scarcity made the farmers worry about their crops. | Scarcity is a fast animal that lives in the desert. | The shop was full of bread, so there was a scarcity of loaves.
exam: What does «food scarcity» mean? | *Too little food for everyone | A large meal for a big family | A festival where people share food | Food that tastes very sweet
